---
/**
 * Signal — first biology-lens concept at Interactive scale.
 * What crosses or is exchanged between living units after Metabolism.
 * Order: Single (Gene → Boundary → Cell → Metabolism) → Signal → Recognition → Coupling.
 * Keep inline tags on one line with outer spaces (Astro whitespace).
 * No em-dashes in public copy.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Signal | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="min-h-[50vh] flex flex-col justify-center pt-28 pb-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">
					Biology lens · Interactive Identity
				</div>
				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tighter leading-[0.95] mb-6 text-white">
					Signal
				</h1>
				<p class="text-xl text-white/50 font-light leading-relaxed mb-6">
					What one living unit releases or transmits so that another can be affected across a boundary:
					the elementary event of interaction between Cells.
				</p>
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/20 bg-amber-500/[0.04] p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Status:</strong> Working concept under the biology lens.
						Primary science reading: intercellular signaling / cell communication.
						Analogy, not isomorphism. Follows Single-scale Metabolism; precedes Recognition and Coupling.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Definition</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">Exchange across membranes.</h2>
				<p>
					In biology, cells do not only maintain themselves in isolation.
					They emit and receive <strong class="text-white/85">signals</strong>: molecules, electrical events, mechanical cues
					that carry information or force across the space between living units.
				</p>
				<p>
					In Identity Engineering, <strong class="text-white/85">Signal</strong> names that elementary interactive event under the biology lens.
					After
					<a href="/framework/metabolism" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Metabolism</a>
					has prepared a Cell to process and release,
					Signal is what actually crosses or is offered at the
					<a href="/framework/boundary" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Boundary</a>
					toward another living unit.
				</p>
				<p>
					Operationally this is the closest biology-lens counterpart to the framework and OS notion of
					<strong class="text-white/85">Interaction Signal</strong>: a structured act that can be admitted, rejected, or partially applied
					under membrane policy, and that can leave a geometric trace in the receiver.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Signal is</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">An interactive event:</strong> something offered or transmitted from one Cell toward another (or into a shared medium).
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Boundary-crossing content:</strong> not the membrane itself, but what the membrane may pass, block, or transform.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Input to another metabolism:</strong> a received signal can be metabolized into geometry, state change, or further signaling.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">First step of Interactive scale:</strong> before stable Coupling, there is at least a signal event.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Signal is not</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Recognition.</strong>
						Recognition decides how a signal is classified and whether it may act.
						Signal is the event being classified. Recognition follows as the next concept.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Coupling.</strong>
						Coupling is sustained structural or functional linkage between units.
						A signal can be one-shot; coupling is ongoing relation.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Metabolism.</strong>
						Metabolism is the internal process of one Cell.
						Signal is what leaves or arrives at the membrane in relation to another unit.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not the full relationship.</strong>
						One signal does not yet make a bond, a collective, or mutual ownership.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not a claim that all identity interaction is molecular.</strong>
						Intercellular signaling is the science reading. The framework maps structure: discrete interactive events across boundaries.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Order in the biology lens</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">From Single into Interactive</h2>
				<ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-3 text-lg">
					<li>Single: Gene → Boundary → Cell → Metabolism</li>
					<li><strong class="text-white/85">Signal</strong> — elementary exchange event</li>
					<li>Recognition (next) — how the receiver classifies and admits</li>
					<li>Coupling (after) — sustained link built from repeated, recognized exchange</li>
				</ol>
				<p>
					Signal answers: <em class="text-white/75">what crosses between living units?</em>
					Recognition will answer: <em class="text-white/75">who or what is allowed to act?</em>
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Engineering</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What we work on</h2>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Make signals explicit:</strong> what is being sent, by whom, toward whom, under what claim?
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Separate event from bond:</strong> do not treat every message as Coupling or as shared Identity.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Respect Boundary on both sides:</strong> sending and receiving are membrane events, not automatic takeover of the other Cell.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Expect metabolic consequence:</strong> a real signal changes the receiver's process, or it was only noise.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-400/[0.04] p-6 text-base">
					<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/80">Science reading</div>
					<p>
						Primary discipline: <strong class="text-white/80">intercellular signaling / cell communication</strong>
						(ligands, messengers, directed cues between cells).
						Recognition and Coupling complete the Interactive scale next.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-4">
					<a href="/framework/metabolism" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Metabolism</a>
					<a href="/framework/boundary" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Boundary</a>
					<a href="/framework/living-identity" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Living Identity</a>
					<a href="/framework" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition">Framework</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
